\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313830} {:answer/id #uuid "eea50f81-a609-5dd4-97d4-e34cece10fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313880} {:answer/id #uuid "f47e4960-b4d5-5018-96c9-56112e9c7b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313931}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313880} :answer-field/id #uuid "92b52dea-8ebd-59fd-ba10-4790e182f356" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314406} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0809e822-7c07-5342-9864-6c3928f81e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312032} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1286cb-ed57-54d9-895a-f9fc1324b1f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312167} {:answer/id #uuid "4c55aeab-c6e1-5fbc-b2db-4a738d0cf09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312594} {:answer/id #uuid "72b80f7b-088d-51a1-9120-764f5e7af0ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312880} {:answer/id #uuid "7938bdd0-ab46-5b80-9a88-703c52b67232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312944}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312594} :answer-field/id #uuid "bec85f47-7594-555b-98c5-7a111c7fab2e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c36e0e36-a227-5df1-b273-538c9f56de6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-340652" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{1}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ \\\\ &= \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{\\sin }^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & ={b}_{1}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{1} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21c52c11-2a0f-58d6-aff5-fbcff80b806b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312230} {:answer/id #uuid "286e0c18-97d0-532c-bf41-6751830ae151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312282} {:answer/id #uuid "a350f6d6-24d8-5f63-b205-477f47e6d19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313260} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b2f783-0c8d-5f89-9d7f-07e8c45faf2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313411} {:answer/id #uuid "e477c6c9-364e-5141-949d-9701044a0b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313778}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312230} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc086cc-8293-54fb-ab53-553c0b9185e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6adb5300-558b-5171-ae85-ccd08169caac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312814} {:answer/id #uuid "84bf4de8-2de1-5c8d-aa10-e8dc5e05701b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313040} {:answer/id #uuid "b6112b1f-27d0-5ea9-9414-69665412c45e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313389} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d80ee5-4b61-5649-991b-08f557a8dc02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313493} {:answer/id #uuid "ea34fcb0-83d8-5c60-9aab-be6de2adf3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313839} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ab1a37-3aeb-50e5-ac0c-f636df7e8865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313911}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312814} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3676550-2291-58a0-8716-0b0471438972" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21099cf0-6ade-5176-97e2-98b51987b126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312226} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9b48c8-5e3a-5bc2-a5ab-b517fd3e8a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312487} {:answer/id #uuid "5f73d4a2-4ad0-5837-b408-af5ab8f8dfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312737} {:answer/id #uuid "b835c93d-0f3b-59f6-8a79-699819da02b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313406} {:answer/id #uuid "f35dc895-fc13-50f6-aa56-710cb0aafcfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313922}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312737} :answer-field/id #uuid "f825e814-46db-5a49-9ae3-db2a2ad9a646" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dc60bc57-5b9c-5f88-9bc5-5ecffd1981e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-340662" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}-6x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{4}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{4} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ \\\\ &= \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{4}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\sin }^{2}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={b}_{4}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{4} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ff7f5fc-cc6f-5e0c-b620-395c49a0910e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313005}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313005} :answer-field/id #uuid "577a6f0c-c116-5f7b-8ade-da2cef88a8af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ea200d68-1faf-5dc8-85fa-da6a4285c621" :question/math-academy-id "q-340672" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{\\theta }^{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{\\theta }^{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}({\\theta }^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{{\\theta }^{2}}{{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{{\\theta }^{2}}{{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{\\theta }^{2}}{{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{(\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\theta }{{\\theta }^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta })}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{{\\theta }^{2}}{{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =1\\cdot 1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32aa477a-226a-50a2-ac65-fe824c849b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312384} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f9b6d3-a27f-5b9f-a0c0-693e164b0ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313766}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312384} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7573555-7ebf-5def-85a1-017344bfdb54" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314648} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1202e93b-fd14-560f-8df8-54729f2a77a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312104} {:answer/id #uuid "6b81a890-6b38-59cd-abc4-cf2e663efa98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312818} {:answer/id #uuid "78a949f3-c74b-5318-9c91-228ddde7b83c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312934} {:answer/id #uuid "e84b3ead-f27b-5dea-a81a-6392a84196d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313822} {:answer/id #uuid "fe92ebd1-e135-5200-98b2-0c04b81ce55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314008}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312934} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b20dd0-67b2-5ad3-8bdf-d6d827ee7612" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b9c74cb-227d-5548-a6f8-2b43a9ca07b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340675" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the half-angle identity\n\n$$\n{\\cos }^{2}⁡(6x)=\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\cos }^{2}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)+\\frac{1}{24}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(24\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ $\\text{are not orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "300a6bc0-d426-5210-be63-d8b89e5e7331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312362} {:answer/id #uuid "45f62daf-fa33-5f7a-a6a4-171539f67319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312547} {:answer/id #uuid "f1168039-ce04-5311-a57d-4f8370ca946a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313906}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312547} :answer-field/id #uuid "417176c0-be1c-5bf4-a5ae-cc2292c8305e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05382f65-c55a-5bb4-b587-0c3958928506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312008} {:answer/id #uuid "10cfc0ca-af0c-544d-b154-16d8f5920201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312095} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee0d27f-e337-5a80-81eb-5383578be5c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312208} {:answer/id #uuid "4bee694b-d79c-52ae-8451-0132709ecab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312590} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f99d0b-d569-513d-9175-fa5b5c1c5c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313360}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313360} :answer-field/id #uuid "8980bf62-4562-52ea-8399-a7c83096c15b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cc6b217a-5fd4-5ebf-923c-68c576688191" :question/math-academy-id "q-340677" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(0-0)-\\frac{1}{16}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "584f29a0-0c7c-5ebb-9c56-60a0b33fcc06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312682} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac9e27d-dfaf-5f7f-9873-e525c060e22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312698} {:answer/id #uuid "a011eb60-d1a9-5f19-a373-50f8d3ec6e19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313235}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313235} :answer-field/id #uuid "42c0d015-eff7-5922-8599-137d3aa4ef9d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17adb654-0a8e-5c02-8028-22814c1d7436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312141} {:answer/id #uuid "3d164866-cd92-5a95-9b6b-c18a178de576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312468} {:answer/id #uuid "80ab1782-1787-5c00-9d6a-269bccea1ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313011} {:answer/id #uuid "c9105c8c-cdcd-5365-a853-30f9320c1006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313544} {:answer/id #uuid "e602871c-e69e-5150-8116-14f72a5c992d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313793}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312468} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d5ce8e-80a4-5b94-abb2-592093cc78b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5b851434-5f95-5831-8b48-c6fb4f555092" :question/math-academy-id "q-340678" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{18}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(18\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(0-0)+\\frac{1}{18}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0daa087f-f323-5faa-a4e9-604ca35655a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312072} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec12530-fa82-5a17-a031-79a932c12dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312207}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312207} :answer-field/id #uuid "23144716-14d7-5695-8ba6-29c9023690ee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01360f92-7aa0-57d4-94ae-48f679e6d3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311969} {:answer/id #uuid "0a9294e7-86af-5ec9-91da-9b7b9c3babbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312055} {:answer/id #uuid "b896a225-dd54-54b0-a287-c64e84fd2786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313409} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b05747-a692-5a14-91bd-a0c5e65ea7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313804} {:answer/id #uuid "f00630e3-28fe-5d6a-9eb6-0f4d51ed9ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313898}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313898} :answer-field/id #uuid "dad5592b-c4ca-59f6-a22d-0e05b8530ab1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "25666762-6caa-548c-81d4-5ffe0a56d215" :question/math-academy-id "q-340681" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-7\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(-1-(-1))-\\frac{1}{2}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f1588de-106f-5f6d-97dc-672a0201c92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "is convergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312086} {:answer/id #uuid "a8cea846-fe82-5bfb-8014-da7d5501cd2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "is divergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313299} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe4a66c-7a33-56e2-949d-55a89cd1069e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "is divergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313734}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313734} :answer-field/id #uuid "046bb0c1-0962-5a71-a6af-d8683978abb6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44cae5f2-2693-5ce9-97cb-adf784f2ddaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "is divergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312532} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6c2000-a9d0-5340-ba44-9362143b07dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "is convergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313597} {:answer/id #uuid "e75f72a9-a972-5b34-99f1-32c7b46420ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "is divergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313809} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c7301c9-3c7f-57d2-b4c9-e7b5d49f4fb3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314126} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2444b069-348c-50cc-931d-5c7e25857d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312247} {:answer/id #uuid "