 "f1e12e2d-9ac1-56f3-b293-e94794a6a02c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3{(y-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332078} {:answer/id #uuid "f630c36b-13b8-5df3-93c0-7e5b92d1a0cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332110} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e8121f-912f-5a99-bfb1-52ab404e7b28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[3\\sqrt{2+\\frac{3j}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332117} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a4584b-0c14-5528-87ea-17193560ab67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a(t)=⟨8t,-\\frac{3}{16}{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332125} {:answer/id #uuid "fa50c537-badc-5e7b-9916-e9adc6bf5c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332144} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332651 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38593a9c-548d-5b0a-8b13-500fce417de7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330454} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec48359-ca66-5a43-aa3f-fd1b2ed80b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330793} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e2c7a7-5534-5f8d-9666-50887184ad23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331699} {:answer/id #uuid "e1338443-0332-576f-91b4-af64c61839fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331938} {:answer/id #uuid "fd6c096c-bf7b-5938-80e6-6115d33f998f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$f(x)$ does not have any local maxima" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332177}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331938} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1f3ab1c-7d13-5548-8d07-8bdc6170269a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "56c5438a-da5f-5788-885e-7f027b595c02" :question/math-academy-id "q-49024" :question/problem "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{x}$ defined for $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ have a local maximum?" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}{\\ln }^{2}⁡(10)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ on $(0,\\infty )$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)} & =0 \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡x & =1 \\\\ x & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=e$ is a stationary point. Next, to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=1,{e}^{2}$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{(1)^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}({e}^{2}) & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{(e)^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}=-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(0,e)$ | $e$ | $(e,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $1$ |  | ${e}^{2}$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical point.\n\n- At $x=e,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=e$ is a local maximum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=e.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "009d8131-2ffe-5c14-a378-d1f56781bded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{x}+2\\ln ⁡(K|x|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329958} {:answer/id #uuid "3c89723c-b495-521d-8ad7-e34b357b5559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x}+2\\ln ⁡(|K|x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330487} {:answer/id #uuid "7a074152-9317-5da0-b3eb-342d5c464ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+2\\ln ⁡(|K|x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331032} {:answer/id #uuid "a03000cf-9b4c-5aa7-bc81-3a390be00d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{x}+\\ln ⁡(2K|x|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331391} {:answer/id #uuid "e71d945d-91e1-5744-9e87-32bc4829e8a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+(1+\\ln ⁡(K|x|))^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331980}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329958} :answer-field/id #uuid "47f28b39-da74-5b7f-b9d6-861abb2e2dcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "edf6e555-e835-5bc6-9e0b-944e25006b84" :question/math-academy-id "q-49067" :question/problem "What is the antiderivative of ${(1+\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Expanding the binomial and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(1+\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+2\\ln ⁡|x|+\\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{-2+1}+C \\\\  & =x+2\\ln ⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, let's rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant $C,$ we can always write $C=2\\ln ⁡K$ where $K$ is some other positive constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with $2\\ln ⁡|x|$ term, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(1+\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}\\text{d}x & =x-\\frac{1}{x}+2\\ln ⁡|x|+2\\ln ⁡K \\\\  & =x-\\frac{1}{x}+2(\\ln ⁡|x|+\\ln ⁡K) \\\\  & =x-\\frac{1}{x}+2\\ln ⁡(K|x|).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332659 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b827063-1d46-592f-9069-3390743f7989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330049} {:answer/id #uuid "6e43e3f4-8303-527b-ac9c-0202bbca05b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x-2{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330942} {:answer/id #uuid "acc6d2b2-c8da-5516-a0d3-c4774188c11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x-{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331480} {:answer/id #uuid "c08add0e-78e7-54c5-ab17-51b762ee0b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331658} {:answer/id #uuid "dffe2f36-c755-5d60-bf8f-1aebfadb9e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-2{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331928}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330049} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8440b49-5a42-5c64-b1d3-8c392b4f068f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "58be8fc4-bf7c-5658-9dd6-29f09252f095" :question/math-academy-id "q-49075" :question/problem "If ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+1}-4{x}^{3},$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+1}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 4{x}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ea8d40-84bf-534f-8e8c-6302589f6d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\ln ⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330280} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4ddb04-2a0f-541d-8c66-b81a1140bf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ln ⁡|2-\\frac{1}{x}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330472} {:answer/id #uuid "9ecd5285-27bd-58a2-ae63-f8d42089b197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-\\ln ⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331373} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfcaae4-3cd8-5b37-ad78-afba74998213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x-4\\ln ⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332021} {:answer/id #uuid "f6fa8737-41d4-5415-b503-7159707db2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{(2x-\\ln ⁡|x|)}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332021} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a2c34fc-7951-5002-8305-c48283de9967" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3c37bd55-c0e8-559f-80d9-e5fdbb837ece" :question/math-academy-id "q-49100" :question/problem "Find the integral of ${(2-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}$ with respect to $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Expanding the binomial and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(2-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x-4\\ln ⁡|x|+\\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{-2+1}+C \\\\  & =4x-4\\ln ⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b5c003-977b-526c-9170-9794348054d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-2{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330027} {:answer/id #uuid "248f8453-3a33-57da-89df-9bf51e524234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsec} x+4{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330261} {:answer/id #uuid "43e2ebab-bd93-5d5d-a12b-e839363c1d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330558} {:answer/id #uuid "bf520213-de34-5d15-a3a8-4acc7d0a6455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-2{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331646} {:answer/id #uuid "d44450f0-95d3-5bbf-9bc3-9c36dc4e5fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsec} x-4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331833}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330027} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fa5dfcc-f8bf-57f0-80c1-40fef676854d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1473ed23-4c35-5374-b722-df11f2918a3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49129" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-6\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-2{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43890837-0184-542e-bfb0-c8abf26f2d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arcsec} x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330556} {:answer/id #uuid "87f58c01-b83d-5223-a5c6-46b3cb72b81f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331162} {:answer/id #uuid "c6950c18-8dd3-5690-bea9-67e9c321a527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331709} {:answer/id #uuid "d79dbd64-34c7-5d4e-a3a7-0728a5eba915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331856} {:answer/id #uuid "f4449f42-3c0a-590e-aa9c-1d1fc42bb400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332101}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331856} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c19e67a-f86d-502d-a731-a117cbd29d2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7235061c-31e7-5f21-9e2a-41d26e24ad09" :question/math-academy-id "q-49131" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (\\frac{4}{1+{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{4}{1+{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332665 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27b0389e-1d57-5284-9063-eafd54da004e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arcsec} x-9x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330304} {:answer/id #uuid "76836d51-9788-55ab-8819-9f6ac5535b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-9{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331011} {:answer/id #uuid "868330b0-f4a0-5fcd-8886-75cb323c4dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-9x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331145} {:answer/id #uuid "8fb21daf-d4d6-5218-8b4b-ffea684f82e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331224} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a8ea66-f445-58de-98b4-e7a240fb7b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+3{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331882}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331145} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8706d15-624e-5108-a410-67cf897b31bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7f0fd041-ce90-54f7-824e-5b0234fc7192" :question/math-academy-id "q-49133" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (\\frac{6}{1+{x}^{2}}-9)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{6}{1+{x}^{2}}-9)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 9\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-9\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-9x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46505b2f-1953-51c1-89b1-262c3e1e114f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsec} x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330584} {:answer/id #uuid "53ca920a-4368-56bd-b725-1abcf2b6713e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330708} {:answer/id #uuid "61645379-6ba4-5686-88be-a9d0c67ea769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330813} {:answer/id #uuid "927c467d-2be8-5aa7-9b42-5199a503c166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arcsec} x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331254} {:answer/id #uuid "a6184f98-47c2-57d1-922d-d6ecf85d4ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsec} x-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331435}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330584} :answer-field/id #uuid "9269b8e4-4637-529d-ad83-2e10b9866149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "93133dfc-bc5a-589b-9b21-0d9909f27fa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49136" :question/problem "If ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsec} x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15842927-5e4a-5e46-9127-104f316af131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330123} {:answer/id #uuid "41bc032e-a7e4-523f-af57-7bedde2ea236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330533} {:answer/id #uuid "5725f42c-d6dd-585b-b6e2-2c205d9241ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-8\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330730} {:answer/id #uuid "8585560a-8491-5f60-8ffc-92f27c87fff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331134} {:answer/id #uuid "b646879c-4463-5645-8b8e-07c71a52b0f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8x+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331558}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330730} :answer-field/id #uuid "16671cae-c5b7-5203-87f8-f4d93fa21ee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4c5875e3-9603-540e-a71c-3edccf17389a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49150" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-7}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-7}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1-1-7}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)-8}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}+1}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}+1}}-\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C,\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1-\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{8}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x-8\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-8\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c9ce83-9aaa-5bbc-92c6-f95472041250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329973} {:answer/id #uuid "049c34a0-277a-5768-b1ba-dcf00b6c9626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329999} {:answer/id #uuid "604dac49-ce40-5774-b7b2-d3426071a9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330803} {:answer/id #uuid "6738e480-3430-569c-8e90-36c9cab6ba7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330875} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a92f45-3db5-5955-86ae-a7d7d451a755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331873}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329973} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d3c3ef7-7fce-5f66-af7e-9e50cf86171e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "86d311d2-8bd0-5e17-8e5a-a9ebe0fb36ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-49178" :question/problem "![](images/ee/ee37408e644416b0fe2d127703e6c5b531ae469e92d4119436fbb7f2b93ef573.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){|}_{1}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "369018b4-21a2-5279-b4e4-e0d994faa356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(4+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330438} {:answer/id #uuid "4d49b614-fccc-5fc4-8acd-61692054062d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330650} {:answer/id #uuid "79bb46b5-657b-5e59-9f8a-8f247898da0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(4+\\frac{i}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331027} {:answer/id #uuid "c8fe173c-3125-5ea8-922f-c1e62b7d4c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{4i}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331729} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4e2460-6f19-520d-87b3-24241e5bd0ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{4i}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331729} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa584d7-2fe7-5dd9-86c5-ef651980a477" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "439d94f9-ec3e-56ab-9e6d-1c9310dea9c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-49188" :question/problem "What is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{2}^{6}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{6}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={x}^{3},$ the lower bound is $a=2,$ and the upper bound is $b=6.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{6-2}{n}=\\frac{4}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{6}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(2+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(2+\\frac{4i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{4i}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bce47fc-4a4e-5975-bcbb-6e2d49402901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5{(4+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330053} {:answer/id #uuid "16c6b768-7d37-5a0d-b8fc-a322f3e0b24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5{(3+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330142} {:answer/id #uuid "7faf3e18-e1b1-510f-b4ef-e46de7a1da8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5{(4+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331077} {:answer/id #uuid "91a94126-e85f-59e8-9934-c5a7252cf2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5{(1+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331245} {:answer/id #uuid "c8529d5b-cb9d-568b-91b6-e038fbe0ab20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5{(3+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331723}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330142} :answer-field/id #uuid "7819a5ff-1aa2-5893-ad86-8d7fa163b7ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c9fff3a7-0d0a-5629-aea3-7c93f4f9d34c" :question/math-academy-id "q-49192" :question/problem "What is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{3}^{4}5{x}^{2}\\text{d}x\n$$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{4}5{x}^{2}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=5{x}^{2},$ the lower bound is $a=3$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-3}{n}=\\frac{1}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}5{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(3+i\\cdot \\frac{1}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(3+\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & =\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5{(3+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16967b2e-35be-56f8-a2bd-46bafdc6d569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330139} {:answer/id #uuid "5de0f056-6523-57e5-99b1-59567f1c94bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330789} {:answer/id #uuid "abbd65db-88ba-5df3-b320-a83e8b75b149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331474} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7dc28d-da0d-56af-8ee7-8921352c7d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332024} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2a62f8-fca2-5193-9d84-ab3e572a3169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332175}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331474} :answer-field/id #uuid "184faa6d-41f3-52b0-b12d-719ec62fd475" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cac5c79c-f0a3-5733-9707-6baf8522f229" :question/math-academy-id "q-49221" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3+1}}{-3+1}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{(-2)}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{(-1)^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(-4)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332680 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c83a7ec-f4a3-5465-b3ea-7f73e1be5c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330060} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1735b0-161b-5bb3-a8da-4c53bf529b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330177} {:answer/id #uuid "25cb08c7-53cd-5ff4-8dde-81922d7dfb9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330276} {:answer/id #uuid "a13530d6-c905-5197-bf5d-171c4d769236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331400} {:answer/id #uuid "bff35d00-c968-5ff8-b9d9-70c7b1da187c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331652}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331400} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbc12171-5296-52ad-9167-20208afcbe5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "08240266-d5ae-5cea-bad2-40e75e833a24" :question/math-academy-id "q-49223" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{x}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5+1}}{-5+1}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4}}{(-4)}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{4}}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{(-1)^{4}}-\\frac{1}{(-2)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332681 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1520edf6-93bb-5db6-9128-f81756520d8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+e)$ and $b={e}^{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330118} {:answer/id #uuid "34612814-166e-5d51-b2d8-255a56c01f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $b={e}^{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330413} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4d58cd-e443-52da-913e-f6feabf466de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+e)$ and $b=2e$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330759} {:answer/id #uuid "90479fe6-a4ca-56f9-9289-46966e3a10b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+e)$ and $b=e+1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331234} {:answer/id #uuid "eafb8eca-ec9c-5930-b366-56e28ce03054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $b=2e$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332011}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332011} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c43ef92-1fe4-5da5-ae81-e8c45f540023" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "be4620a0-c65c-5bd5-aaf3-d3285dc13e62" :question/math-academy-id "q-49235" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{e}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+\\frac{ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=e.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{e}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{e}{n}=\\frac{b-e}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=2e.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{i}=e+\\frac{ie}{n}$ and $f({x}_{i})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{i}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{e}^{2e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+\\frac{ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $b=2e.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b7cf8f-bcce-5eb2-9e2b-d634b7d1d4f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330099} {:answer/id #uuid "12b7179f-1b92-5e99-a7b9-29de6e25a71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330109} {:answer/id #uuid "9ed74260-8967-54c8-a982-79627134f8f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331374} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e94cb7-1494-5d46-b1b3-78ae25482c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331719} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e590e3-3337-590b-a068-6ead06d74561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331874}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330099} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac043f6d-7a72-52c6-9ca4-b976607baf36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b31b1059-0bef-5971-a208-8d252626b22e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49272" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identities $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\n$$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332693 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48b77ad6-2790-5fb9-ac75-c531ab004c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330601} {:answer/id #uuid "8a571c79-fa20-5257-bd99-b3a3310b2bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331178} {:answer/id #uuid "8b31c3cf-dd75-5df7-9b83-aa025a1ed598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331185} {:answer/id #uuid "9549f7ba-8509-55bb-ac17-34f5f78e130c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331274} {:answer/id #uuid "d75920df-cc3f-5f99-8620-29d4802abe07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330601} :answer-field/id #uuid "075617b4-7fd7-5fe0-bba2-6157b32a856f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a78f750a-573a-57da-b09b-e012074904df" :question/math-academy-id "q-49284" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{\\cos }^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{\\cos }^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\n$$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{\\cos }^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332694 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25b0850f-fa25-5b05-9950-7e0e634c06c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330275} {:answer/id #uuid "61fe0262-2ac7-5c54-8be0-54f9f416208b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330827} {:answer/id #uuid "6a515304-6a32-5abe-a406-870f9a6a8691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330905} {:answer/id #uuid "82b1f11b-9dc9-5745-9d60-f88f832c5e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331105} {:answer/id #uuid "e429182d-57f1-592c-ae86-682900ce93a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331962}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331105} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ee28e4-2550-58c8-bf71-43555f4f9c46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a41d63bd-84eb-5f5c-b954-12d95e773df1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49286" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f8e4dc1dff5673d8fc95375f9632f43bc4942335899e0e6dad11e8693bd6599.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=5{\\sin }^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi .$ The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=5{\\sin }^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi $ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{\\sin }^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{\\sin }^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={\\sin }^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{\\sin }^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\sin }^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}([\\pi -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )]-[0-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11dbbe25-f605-5318-ad46-dc495bb13c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330105} {:answer/id #uuid "ab70ca2b-b076-587e-a88e-1d10fb8a7498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331469} {:answer/id #uuid "bf37637a-7683-56c4-bb69-925e9cc147a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331645} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d35bf0-51c8-56cd-8c8d-1bcbce77b9af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331802} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ef6fe2-0740-5343-acd8-b64c29efd3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330105} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0499ae3-ea01-5507-9906-ec2b8d72e827" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "489c69ce-d415-5c5f-8b91-c246b0512a1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49294" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dcc78643dd44633f778d954de32a955dc5803abf7dc059c30bbbda97bc35413f.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{\\cos }^{2}⁡x+{\\sin }^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2{\\cos }^{2}⁡x+{\\sin }^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${\\cos }^{2}⁡x+{\\sin }^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\cos }^{2}⁡x+{\\sin }^{2}⁡x & ={\\cos }^{2}⁡x+({\\sin }^{2}⁡x+{\\cos }^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={\\cos }^{2}⁡x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${\\cos }^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{\\cos }^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{\\cos }^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({\\cos }^{2}⁡x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }[\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi +3\\pi )-(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\pi +\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{9\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027c7b2d-b6da-57b7-bebe-fb4037a57c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi (8\\pi +1)}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329986} {:answer/id #uuid "5edb996b-f64a-5b21-a842-f045e68a17ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\pi }^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330794} {:answer/id #uuid "694123a1-c921-511a-acce-7bbd45a25a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11{\\pi }^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330892} {:answer/id #uuid "992e5b44-a5b7-5d52-9616-a516782a146b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi (3\\pi -2)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331319} {:answer/id #uuid "c067d35b-09ff-52a9-b0d8-b519ceb90554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331656}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331319} :answer-field/id #uuid "518cab6c-8aef-56e1-9322-1acdbcc19ee8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e50b0ecc-a7e1-5f2d-884d-81b7bbf09d3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-49299" :question/problem "![](images/20/20844131c3d35b02f0ba7c6567b7765a54f0909e63ee309181dd5a25248dbfd5.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=-2{\\sin }^{2}⁡x+2x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=-2{\\sin }^{2}⁡x+2x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-2{\\sin }^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{\\sin }^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1=-2{\\sin }^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-2{\\sin }^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-x+{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi -\\pi +{\\pi }^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{{2}^{2}}] \\\\  & =-\\pi +{\\pi }^{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}-4\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}+2\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3\\pi -2)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332700 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9279f99b-07e2-5a92-8769-3475c1ea0dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-2t+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331253} {:answer/id #uuid "b87fe0d4-fd32-5c26-8c08-409e0cde8ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P(t)=6{t}^{2}-2t+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331580} {:answer/id #uuid "c30a6019-ea0e-584b-a717-eb7354915f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-2t+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331684} {:answer/id #uuid "d274239f-73bc-5926-8b40-d5d950a40492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}+2t+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331817} {:answer/id #uuid "fad18f17-4495-5b82-8fa3-74b112c945db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P(t)=6{t}^{2}-2t+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332152}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331253} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ce4ab34-42a1-5b78-9fe0-f9fc91c4a733" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7f052148-475f-5e9d-b934-2204e76a0ded" :question/math-academy-id "q-49315" :question/problem "A bicycle tire has a pressure of $6\\,\\text{psi}.$ It is being inflated, and the pressure is increasing at a rate of $4t\\,\\text{psi}$ per second, where $t$ is a time, in seconds, since the start of the inflation. The tire has a slow puncture that reduces pressure at a rate of $(t+2)\\,\\text{psi}$ per second. Identify an expression for $P(t),$ the total pressure in the tire at any time $t\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $p(t)=4t-(t+2)=3t-2$ be the rate at which the pressure in the tire is changing. Note that we subtract $(t+2)$ to indicate the rate at which the pressure is decreasing.\n\nLet $P(T)$ be the pressure in the tire after $T$ seconds. Then, using our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nP(T)=P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T) & =P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6+{\\int }_{0}^{T}(3t-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6+{(\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-2t)|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =6+\\frac{3}{2}{T}^{2}-2T \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{T}^{2}-2T+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-2t+6.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32af58e6-09c6-533d-a92e-1ea07319319c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330398} {:answer/id #uuid "519f3d8e-bbb5-5684-a860-614dedf022a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330689} {:answer/id #uuid "90d39998-b7dd-53c3-91f5-aa4c5a2bc8d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331237} {:answer/id #uuid "cae02916-1d5c-5803-9ea9-fb4706849276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331747} {:answer/id #uuid "df7c8635-900a-5696-8f95-b62857b9e80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331923}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330398} :answer-field/id #uuid "421ac1f8-6581-569e-a080-7d1a5bcf5184" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "06189516-15f6-57fc-9a99-e7cebf7baa9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-49353" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|rr} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 \\\\ \\hline  & 2 & -1\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}=2-\\frac{1}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(2-\\frac{1}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}2\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{|}_{2}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =2(3-2)-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-1|) \\\\  & =2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332704 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39877dcd-c15f-5b42-9992-628fd69aa8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330466} {:answer/id #uuid "4d37ea75-59a6-53b7-8119-27c921f17e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330649} {:answer/id #uuid "78fde374-d249-56e5-8ed2-413b17b19765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331025} {:answer/id #uuid "bde7299b-9c7d-563b-a909-63879e3087e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331631} {:answer/id #uuid "fae341a7-c701-5ce9-8756-3f3183adee01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332153}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331631} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd8664ab-82c6-5935-885b-4704ea3140b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ec1f8b08-73c8-5230-ba02-f32931218a96" :question/math-academy-id "q-49354" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|rr} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 \\\\  & ↓ & -10 \\\\ \\hline  & 5 & -3\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+7}{x+2}=5-\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5-\\frac{3}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332705 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c4acae-b369-5f9b-8ab6-963eb8877cae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330257} {:answer/id #uuid "33963c3d-8e28-5e8a-8a4d-093fcb4cb9f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330407} {:answer/id #uuid "3f105bea-c32e-589f-8c75-66f47fa62806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330509} {:answer/id #uuid "ad881229-1a77-57ac-84f9-baa044032197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331487} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d64f50-21be-5975-8c1b-ab28d7fb0be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331659} :answer-field/id #uuid "5093329b-485c-593c-9a8f-8d21ad28ebee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7806e71e-9cb7-55be-836c-04e6fc97f767" :question/math-academy-id "q-49357" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x+1}{4(x+\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|rr} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4} & 1 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\hline  & 1 & \\frac{3}{4}\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})} & =1+\\frac{\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{3}{4(x+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{3}{4x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (1+\\frac{3}{4x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\int \\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[x+\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "228ee8e3-4cbc-54ca-86e0-41d6984f52f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|(1+x)(1-x)|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330248} {:answer/id #uuid "415b24a1-a0a1-566e-804a-10c3a545d297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|(1+x)(1-x)|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330529} {:answer/id #uuid "4af1094c-11cd-5b21-a560-c386722e9007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|\\frac{1+x}{1-x}|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330628} {:answer/id #uuid "5e33cd57-a4d3-57fa-af23-86332f408cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|\\frac{1+x}{1-x}|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330791} {:answer/id #uuid "86a4a011-da14-5843-825b-84a1ae516e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|\\frac{1+x}{1-x}|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331147} :answer-field/id #uuid "d573eb9f-5b4a-5c4d-be89-c86d1a19944c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1dc5a85a-4afe-5495-af86-22c90f6982a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-49360" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int (\\frac{1}{1+x}+\\frac{1}{1-x})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$ Assume that $K$ is an arbitrary positive constant." :question/worked-solution "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{1+x}+\\frac{1}{1-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{1+x}{1-x}|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|\\frac{1+x}{1-x}|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c11ff0-71d5-5bee-aae5-8b0816d61754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330128} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2cfdeb-9842-58b1-b828-74e45464f343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3\\sqrt[4]{1-5s}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330797} {:answer/id #uuid "61a59c95-07ff-5f5f-971c-f9bd9ea7288e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{7}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330822} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6dd38f-46e2-5f77-9d50-cb6ab9cd68d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331062} {:answer/id #uuid "c7305939-90b2-595f-b633-babd5a276440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331062} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f47b77-e5fb-5327-8f5a-bf4eb1d0b728" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "44b08892-d784-5133-8162-d9d2c70e3c9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-49393" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{(3-5s)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}s=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (3-5s)^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=3-5s.$ Then differentiating with respect to $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}s}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}s=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3-5s)^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}s & =\\int {u}^{-2/3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1/3}{u}^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{u}^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}(3-5s)^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C] & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[(3-5s)^{1/3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}(3-5s)^{-2/3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3-5s)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}(3-5s)^{-2/3}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =(3-5s)^{-2/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{(3-5s)^{2}}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332710 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a02435-6aa5-5493-be91-0fce8cc404bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329971} {:answer/id #uuid "6d10e2b7-53a2-5a33-9ee8-5a7b58667f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330927} {:answer/id #uuid "b93fd321-dc00-5315-b863-cd7155d5f7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331589} {:answer/id #uuid "c322c7d1-1c7c-5702-9c0d-9e8209d203ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331686} {:answer/id #uuid "f7895fe5-aafe-554b-8d81-1da1c93eaec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332123}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329971} :answer-field/id #uuid "e379815b-aeca-5008-b3af-c97853ca491f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "72f64856-0d6e-5756-9e66-30ca70000360" :question/math-academy-id "q-49398" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|rr} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\ \\hline  & 1 & 1\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{x+3}=1+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1+\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{-2}^{0}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-2+3|) \\\\  & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332711 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa643cd-cab1-5ade-865c-2ba78686b638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330221} {:answer/id #uuid "3d97a4ee-fa2a-5fae-b5fa-2715e7131749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330492} {:answer/id #uuid "7e463ea7-19e4-529c-b870-2b3a0b40c9e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331060} {:answer/id #uuid "e6a66305-917b-5ac4-9c21-63b458684b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331977} {:answer/id #uuid "ee55835d-1b3a-5379-b60e-da7bd2450951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332042}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331977} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca36d191-da6d-5a33-8d37-58b4562c2c2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae52f11d-c818-5b04-9e5a-10577e3d8339" :question/math-academy-id "q-49404" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{x+3}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|rr} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\  & ↓ & 4 \\\\ \\hline  & 1 & 7\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{x-4}=1+\\frac{7}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+3}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+\\frac{7}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31fde650-5d1d-58f5-b17c-c6192af91df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330388} {:answer/id #uuid "648fc0d3-ddc8-5822-876f-641db6f2eb54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330846} {:answer/id #uuid "69558ffe-1dd1-5e52-9f4c-43a0cb12a0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330893} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1716a6-3122-5ceb-87fe-f90b1c0baddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331768} {:answer/id #uuid "d98c0aae-cedb-5226-be00-6b72a7ecaa4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331768} :answer-field/id #uuid "43c2b151-9641-543a-a9e4-863ccfeeb6ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77cb94ec-923d-5f13-9587-b73868bfbd09" :question/math-academy-id "q-49411" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{3x-2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|rr} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\ \\hline  & 3 & -5\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x-2}{x+1}=3-\\frac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x-2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332713 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e3f97f3-b74f-54fb-bb2e-7bf97172b5d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-6x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330501} {:answer/id #uuid "47202dd9-bb4d-509e-a40c-df75d9c66c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330590} {:answer/id #uuid "77240f28-38ec-564e-a11f-346e26fc3fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331014} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e56361-768c-573f-8804-8ea77dc13e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331831} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1c14e5-9fdd-5e9f-b022-0f739d63b156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-4x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332173}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331831} :answer-field/id #uuid "d829abe4-515c-5bca-86e5-8cfeedb29672" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8facc4fe-78b5-55cc-b01a-0ed033eb2116" :question/math-academy-id "q-49415" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|rrr} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 5 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 & -6 \\\\ \\hline  & 1 & 2 & -5\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}=x+2-\\frac{5}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (x+2-\\frac{5}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332714 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71c6acf6-7882-50ca-b3f2-4cc1c2525e0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330972} {:answer/id #uuid "9f5ac57b-b62f-5ed2-92c5-d836155b7835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331380} {:answer/id #uuid "d5727005-35a1-58d8-a6fc-edcf6cc1162a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+3x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331842} {:answer/id #uuid "db48c127-f38d-54be-87d3-869df9d1ab19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331891} {:answer/id #uuid "de46956b-13c2-5281-bea2-a8ae42e1139f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331915}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331915} :answer-field/id #uuid "7743b987-aac7-582b-bac2-e1cc0926a4df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f73bd1c4-b9fa-52db-a8ab-fa70bf82958b" :question/math-academy-id "q-49421" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|rrrr} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\  & ↓ & -2 & 10 & -18 \\\\ \\hline  & 1 & -5 & 9 & -16\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}={x}^{2}-5x+9-\\frac{16}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}-5x+9-\\frac{16}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+9\\int \\text{d}x-16\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
